  "body": "Fork synced at v0.20.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 71).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe 2D Pocket can now cut only what a larger previous tool left. It uses the rest generator of #1446 (`machining2d::rest_pocket`).\n\n- **Parameter.** `OpParams::Pocket` has a new optional `rest` group: previous tool diameter, its corner radius, the stock it left on the walls, and the rest allowance. `None` is off. Off is the default and the plain pocket.\n- **Undoable edit.** You change the group through `EditOperationParams`. Undo and redo restore it.\n- **Project file.** The key is `rest` (an object). A file without the key reads as off, so the file version does not change.\n- **Stamp.** The stamp writes the group (byte `0xD7`) only when it is on. Each value of the group changes the stamp.\n- **Generation.** When the group is on, generation calls `rest_pocket`. Its note (\"rest machining trusts the entered previous tool ...\") goes into the path notes.\n- **Refusals by name, in the generator's own words, when you make, edit or retool the operation** (not only at Generate):\n  - a previous tool that is not larger than the operation's tool (new `rest_gate`, run from `tool_gate` and from the edit);\n  - a value that is negative or not finite, a previous tool diameter that is 0 or less, or a corner radius larger than the previous tool's radius;\n  - the Zigzag or Adaptive strategy;\n  - pre-drilled entry with rest machining on (`REST_PREDRILLED`). `rest_pocket` does not read the holes, and the program must not drop a user setting without saying so.\n- **Motion crate.** `RestParams` has a new `validate_alone` (the checks that do not need a tool, plus \"the previous tool diameter must be positive\"). The strategy check moved into a public `rest_strategy`. Its text did not change.\n- **MCP.** `edit_operation` sets the group (`\"rest\": null` turns it off). There is a new row in the camcraft-mcp skill. Area: mcp.\n- **Not in this PR: the dialog group.** It is not part of \"Done means\", and it needs before/after screenshots and the UI gate. The page keeps the group as it is when you apply the page. Follow-up: #1815.\n\n## How tested\n\nThe new pinning tests are in `crates/app/tests/rest_pocket.rs`:\n- `the_rest_pass_cuts_only_the_corners_posts_and_matches_its_golden`: the fixture is a 60 x 40 pocket with 3 mm corners. A 12 mm end mill roughs it, then a 4 mm end mill does the rest pass. The golden is `pocket_rest_corners.cl`. All cuts stay in the corners. The program posts and the verification report is clean.\n- `read_against_the_simulated_roughing_pass`: the roughing pass is simulated first on the stock dexel grid. Then:\n  - no rapid of the rest pass hits stock;\n  - every plunge goes down on floor that is already clear, and its rim touches stock for no more than one level;\n  - all 8 rings (4 corners x 2 levels) cut stock, and air is less than half of each ring.\n- `the_group_is_an_undoable_edit_and_the_project_file_keeps_it`\n- `a_previous_tool_that_is_not_larger_is_refused_by_name_at_the_edit_and_the_retool` (edit, create and retool)\n- `values_and_strategies_the_rest_pass_cannot_run_are_refused_by_name`\n- `mcp_sets_refuses_undoes_and_saves_the_group` (set, refuse, save, reopen, null, undo)\n\nOther tests:\n- `operation::rest_op_tests::the_rest_group_moves_the_stamp`\n- `crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs`: a new case for a 0 mm previous tool.\n\nMutation check: I deleted each new refusal line, the stamp line and the generation line one at a time, ran the test that pins it, and saw it fail. Then I restored the file and compared it with a backup. All 11 failed when deleted and were restored byte for byte: the motion \"must be positive\" check, rest_op's three refusals, sane's `named_refusal` and `is_sane` lines, `rest_gate` in `tool_gate`, `rest_gate` in the edit, the refusal arm inside `rest_gate`, the `0xD7` stamp block, and the `rest_pocket` call in generation.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick` plans almost the whole workspace for this diff, so I ran the touched suites by name instead (motion: lib, rest2d, machining2d, predrilled_entry, corner_arc_radius, optimal_load, solid_law; app: lib, rest_pocket, golden_cl, arc_turn_params, predrilled_entry, project_roundtrip, roughing2d, adaptive_trochoid, mcp, mcp_pockets, pocket_recognition, operations, commands_undo, tool_gate, tool_law, verify, solid_law_goldens, heights, tilt, corner_blend, climb_direction, area_controls, pick_agnostic, pocket_overhead, units_in_refusals, lead_approach, level_links, whole_model_pocket, recorded_post_streams; ui: lib, edge_loop_pick, operations). All green. Clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-motion, camcraft-app and camcraft-ui (all targets): clean.\n\nThe existing pocket goldens do not change (`golden_cl`, `adaptive_trochoid`, `roughing2d` and the others in the list above).\n\n## What I did not test\n\n- I did not run the program on a machine, and I did not take screenshots (there is no UI change).\n- Two things I measured but did not fix, because they are generator behaviour and not part of this slice:\n  - The inner leg of each corner ring crosses floor that the 12 mm tool already cleared: 6.7 mm of a 14.8-15.3 mm ring. Follow-up: #1816.\n  - On each level, 2 of the 4 corner plunges touch rest material at the rim. The tool axis is over cleared floor. Entry from cleared space belongs to #1490.\n- All of these are feed moves, so they cost time, not safety.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1489-rest-pocket-param.md`.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket rest machining: cut only what a larger previous tool left (previous tool entered by hand); undoable, saved in the project, set through MCP; a previous tool that is not larger is refused by name (#1489)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1489\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nProcess change: yes\n",
